## Workflow Policy

_Generated from `config.workflow_policy` — edit the config, not this block. Changes made here are
overwritten on the next regeneration._

Each line below renders from one policy field; the init flow substitutes the placeholder with prose
matching the configured value.

- **Writing tests** — {{WORKFLOW_POLICY_TEST_AUTHORING}}
  _(`test_authoring`: `allowed` → write tests as part of the work | `ask` → propose tests and wait
  for approval before writing them)_
- **Running tests** — {{WORKFLOW_POLICY_TEST_EXECUTION}}
  _(`test_execution`: `allowed` | `ask` | `user_only` → never run tests; the user runs them and
  reports results)_
- **Servers and app processes** — {{WORKFLOW_POLICY_SERVER_LIFECYCLE}}
  _(`server_lifecycle`: `allowed` | `ask` | `user_only` → never start, stop, restart, or kill
  servers or app processes)_
- **Probing endpoints** — {{WORKFLOW_POLICY_ENDPOINT_PROBING}}
  _(`endpoint_probing`: `allowed` | `ask` | `user_only` → no `curl`/HTTP calls against running
  services; inspect data through the project's console/runner instead)_
- **Creating documentation** — {{WORKFLOW_POLICY_DOCUMENTATION_CREATION}}
  _(`documentation_creation`: `allowed` | `ask` → do not create README/summary/report files unless
  asked)_
- **Creating tickets** — {{WORKFLOW_POLICY_TICKET_CREATION}}
  _(`ticket_creation`: `proactive` → create tickets whenever work is described |
  `followups_only` → only for substantial multi-session follow-ups; small fixes ride along on an
  existing ticket | `explicit_only` → only when the user asks)_
- **Closing tickets** — {{WORKFLOW_POLICY_TICKET_CLOSE}}
  _(`ticket_close`: `auto` → mark DONE and archive without asking | `ask` → propose closure and wait
  for the user)_
